        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Financial Accounting",
        "topic": "Depreciation Methods",
        "question_type": "Practical",
        "exam_year": "2000",
        "question_text": "<p>A machine costing \u20b550,000 has an estimated useful life of 5 years and a scrap value of \u20b55,000. Calculate the annual depreciation charge using the <b>straight-line method</b>.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The straight-line depreciation formula is:<br><b>Annual Depreciation = (Cost - Scrap Value) / Useful Life</b>.<br>Substitute the values: (\u20b550,000 - \u20b55,000) / 5 = <b>\u20b59,000</b> per year.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
